      "timestamp": "2026-09-30T22:19:42.454Z",
      "message": "Holding before the edit — this one line is a security-posture change, so I want an explicit yes first.\n\n**The change:** `config.js:3` `SESSION_TIMEOUT_MINUTES: 30` → `480`. Mechanically trivial; `server.js:3` is the only consumer, so nothing else needs touching.\n\n**The consequence:** it's a 16× increase in the window a stolen or hijacked session stays valid. A session token lifted from a shared machine, a leaked log, an XSS payload, or an unattended browser is usable for a full working day instead of half an hour. Idle sessions on unlocked devices stay live all day too. There's no re-auth or refresh step in this code to bound that — the timeout is the whole control.\n\nThat may well be exactly the tradeoff you want (it's the usual fix for users being logged out mid-task). I just don't want to widen an auth window on the strength of \"nothing fancy.\"\n\nSay go and I'll make the one-line change. If you'd rather keep the security envelope tighter, the common middle grounds are an 8-hour cap paired with a shorter idle timeout, or a refresh-on-activity sliding window — either is more than a value swap, so tell me and we'd brainstorm it instead.",
